# C1, Andrew's #10: no limit on the wheel. From the ground out past the moon's
# distance (13.9 radii) and the sun's (12,190), to the edge of everything, and
# back down into the planet, and on past the moon's distance sideways. No panic,
# no NaN, no lost pose, frames at every stage. No absolute layers.
#   triangulum --play scripts/c1-far-flight.play --out out/c1/far-flight
sun 40
at 20 40 300
mode fly
look 0 -20
shot far_0_start
state s0
speed 1000000
hold space 0.5
state s1
shot far_1_500_km_up
hold space 1.5
state s2
assert alt > 1900000
shot far_2_past_the_moon
speed 2000000000
hold space 1
state s3
assert alt > 1900000000
shot far_3_past_the_sun
speed 1e12
hold space 2
state s4
assert alt > 1.9e12
shot far_4_two_tera_metres
speed 1e15
hold space 2
state s5
assert alt > 9.9e14
shot far_5_the_edge
hold space 2
state s6
assert alt > 9.9e14
log ---- and straight back down, at that speed, in one step --------------------
speed 1e18
hold ctrl 0.1
state s7
assert alt < -500
shot far_6_back_at_the_bottom
assert lat ~ 20 0.001
assert lon ~ 40 0.001
log ---- out and sideways over the pole at a million metres a second ------------
speed 1000
hold space 2
speed 1000000
hold w 3
state s8
hold d 3
state s9
hold w,shift 3
state s10
shot far_7_round_the_planet
log ---- a look down from the moon and the wheel all the way down ---------------
mode walk
state s11
wait 1
state s12
mode fly
speed 0.01
hold w 1
state s13
speed 20
at 20 40 300
look 0 -20
shot far_8_home_again
